        "header": "2Architecture",
        "images": [
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.24815/2609.24815v3/framework_revised.png",
                "caption": "Figure 1:Autoregressive Diffusion Model Framework.Uranus combines an outer causal autoregressive loop with an inner latent flow-matching diffusion process.\nAt rollout steptt, persistent multi-view reference RGB frames and clean history latent frames are encoded together with text instructions, four future joint configurations aligned with the output RGB timestamps, and per-RGB-frame camera geometry.\nConditioned on this context, the DiT iteratively transports Gaussian noise toward the next clean multi-view latent, which is decoded by the pretrained VAE into a synchronized RGB chunk of four frames per view.\nThe generated observation is then appended to the history and reused as context for subsequent predictions, enabling joint-trajectory-conditioned long-horizon rollout.",
                "position": 549
            },
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.24815/2609.24815v3/Uranus_Figure2_spelling_fixed.png",
                "caption": "Figure 2:Overview of Uranus.Uranus is a multi-view image-to-video diffusion transformer for interactive robot simulation. It autoregressively predicts future multi-camera observations from encoded reference RGB frames and clean history latent frames, future joint-position trajectories rendered as temporally aligned skeleton maps, camera geometry encoded by Plücker ray embeddings, and text prompts. For each generated latent frame, four ordered RGB-time condition maps are compressed into one latent-time token slice by learned temporal–spatial projections and added to the video-latent tokens at the DiT input. Clean context tokens are assigned denoising timestep zero, while the current target latent frame is generated from noise with its actual diffusion timestep. Reference anchors use fixed prefix RoPE positions, whereas generated history and target latent frames use a separate latent-time index starting from zero.",
                "position": 559
            },
